BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eleanor the Great
DTSTART:20251001T230000Z
DTEND:20251002T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20251001T230000Z
UID:gRLj5IKGTk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nOscar nominee June Squibb (SIFF 2
 024 Honoree) stars in Scarlett Johansson’s thoughtful\, provocative\, an
 d very funny feature directorial debut\, about a nonagenarian who passes h
 erself off as a Holocaust survivor.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-thea
 ters/eleanor-the-great
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Quality Ski Time Film Tour
DTSTART:20251007T020000Z
DTEND:20251007T045000Z
DTSTAMP:20251007T020000Z
UID:i8pDY2ZKcM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 150 mins (2h30m)\n\nPresented by Salomon Doors: 6:00
 pm Ski movies will forever be a part of ski culture. Nothing else can matc
 h the community and excitement created by watching films with friends. So\
 , why would you settle for just one film? Get stoked for winter with us 
 by watching several films\, each showcasing different stories\, athletes a
 nd types of skiing.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/quality-ski
 -time-film-tour-2025
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ascent (1977)
DTSTART:20251106T020000Z
DTEND:20251106T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20251106T020000Z
UID:nZf50CJ5pm
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club Shepitko’s emo
 tionally overwhelming final film won the Golden Bear at the 1977 Berlin Fi
 lm Festival and has been hailed around the world as the finest Soviet film
  of its decade. Set during World War II's darkest days\, The Ascent follow
 s the path of two peasant soldiers\, cut off from their troop\, who trudge
  through the snowy backwoods of Belarus seeking refuge among villagers. Th
 eir harrowing trek leads them on a journey of betrayal\, heroism\, and ult
 imate transcendence.  Introduced by SIFF Cinema Staff Member Adam Plesser
 .\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/the-ascent
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Night of the Hunter (1955)
DTSTART:20251204T020000Z
DTEND:20251204T035500Z
DTSTAMP:20251204T020000Z
UID:m3c3J36K5J
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club Part fairy tale\,
  part Southern gothic horror story\, The Night of the Hunter tells the sto
 ry of a psychopathic preacher who pursues two children who hold the key to
  hidden loot. 70th anniversary screening.  Introduced by SIFF Education 
 Manager Megan Garbayo-López.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events
 /siff-movie-club/the-night-of-the-hunter
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
